        "original_id": "1465b47f-c693-5e2f-8a16-107d0ffdfb56",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Danny Bonaduce, Joseph Bonaduce, Bonnie Franklin, Mackenzie Phillips, Valerie Bertinelli, Cheyenne Haynes\n- TV Shows/Films: One Day at a Time, I Know My Kid's a Star, The Partridge Family, Lies in Plain Sight, The Dick Van Dyke Show\n- Companies/Networks: CBS, Lifetime Movie Network\n- Places: Broomall, Pennsylvania, Indianapolis\n\nFacts:\n- One Day at a Time is an American sitcom that aired on CBS from December 16, 1975, until May 28, 1984.\n- One Day at a Time starred Bonnie Franklin as a divorced mother raising two teenage daughters, played by Mackenzie Phillips and Valerie Bertinelli, in Indianapolis.\n- Danny Bonaduce was born on August 13, 1959, and is an American radio and television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, and former child actor.\n- Danny Bonaduce was born in Broomall, Pennsylvania, and is the son of veteran TV writer and producer Joseph Bonaduce.\n- Joseph Bonaduce worked on The Dick Van Dyke Show and One Day at a Time.\n- I Know My Kid's a Star has Danny Bonaduce as its host and primary judge.\n- Danny Bonaduce is known for being a child actor on the 1970s TV show The Partridge Family.\n- Cheyenne Haynes is known for Lies in Plain Sight on Lifetime Movie Network and for I Know My Kid's a Star.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
